            "transcript": "Good morning, everyone. Thanks for joining so early. Morning. Happy to be here. Shall we start with the plan? So the plan for this quarter is fairly simple. We start with the discovery work, and we keep it short. Um, after that the team moves into design, which takes about six weeks. During design we agree the scope, the data, and the people who own each part. Then build starts, and build is where most of the money goes. Uh, testing runs alongside build for the last three weeks. If testing goes well, we pilot with one site before anyone else. The pilot tells us what we got wrong while it is still cheap to fix. After the pilot we roll out in waves, two sites at a time. Each wave gets a short review, and we change the next wave if we need to. By the end of the year every site should be live. That is the whole plan, more or less. That makes sense. What about the budget, and who signs it off? The board does. Mm-hmm, every quarter. Great. Let us leave it there for today.",
